s9-3-p45 : Block
s9-3-p45 = prose (cons "The code image is quantified over rather than fixed to an isolated block, but **admissibility is an actual argument of the block proof**. The distinction is necessary: the state predicate \(P(s)\) alone cannot constrain an independently quantified code image \(C\). A branch whose target lies outside the block, or a decoder whose result depends on bytes beyond its end, therefore needs an admissibility premise stronger than \(\mathsf{Contains}\). A closed, position-independent straight-line block may use containment alone when the decoder's locality has been proved. The premises of \(P(s)\) include memory permissions, stack and ABI conditions; the transition preserves the immutable code image. Unit trace contracts recover ordinary Hoare-style blocks." nil)
